2. **`apps/web/src/routes/match.tsx`**:
   - **Imports.** Change `import { navigate, paths } from "../net/navigate.ts";` to `import { guardLeaving, navigate, paths } from "../net/navigate.ts";`. Add `import ConfirmLeaveMatch from "../game/ConfirmLeaveMatch.tsx";` after `import Game from "../game/Game.tsx";`.
   - **State and effect.** In `MatchRoute`, put this right after the `#1792` effect that sets `document.title`, before `if (view === null) {`. Copy it exactly:
     ```tsx
     // R2479000: while the match is live, every way off the board (its Back, the browser's Back, any
     // in-app move but a forced one) asks first and names the disconnect grace (§9.5). A finished,
     // voided or refused match has nothing to come back to, so it is left at once.
     const [leaving, setLeaving] = useState<{ leave: () => void } | null>(null);
     const atStake =
       view !== null && view.result === null && match.connection !== "closed" && match.connection !== "refused";
     useEffect(() => {
       if (!atStake) return;
       const release = guardLeaving((leave) => {
         setLeaving({ leave });
       });
       return () => {
         release();
         setLeaving(null);
       };
     }, [atStake]);
     ```
   - **The dialog.** In the last `return`, inside the `app-shell` div and after `<CatalogContext.Provider value={lookup}>{board}</CatalogContext.Provider>`, add:
     ```tsx
     {leaving === null ? null : (
       <ConfirmLeaveMatch
         onStay={() => {
           setLeaving(null);
         }}
         onLeave={leaving.leave}
       />
     )}
     ```
     `onLeave` must be `leaving.leave` itself. Do not call `setLeaving(null)` before it. After a held browser Back the move is a `history.back()`. If the dialog closes first, its back-layer entry is left spent, and that Back would land on the match again.

